--- /dev/null
+++ b/device/asus/p00a/audio/staging/sepolicy/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+No new SELinux types, rules, file labels, permissive domains or exceptions are needed by this stage. Genuine upstream `hal_audio_default` hosts the wrapper and C HAL; platform `hal_audio_server` already grants `audio_device` directory and character access. `/dev/snd/*` must retain platform audio_device labels and audio group DAC permissions. No private calibration, NVRAM, sysfs, GPIO, broad /data or core-domain grants are added. The HAL does not open any such file. Parent must run the complete product neverallow/checkpolicy/secilc checks after integration; static reuse of platform policy is not a full-product pass.
+
+The upstream service init reference is evidence only; `android.hardware.audio.service` supplies its own `init_rc`. Do not install a duplicate service. Its upstream groups/capabilities are inherited platform behavior, not newly added policy in this bundle. Parent should inspect final init/DAC/labels before commissioning.
